1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:07,800
Meet Cowrie — an independent clean-room Rust implementation of Federated Cashu (BLS12-381).

2
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:17,600
Federation security demands client diversity. One shared codebase means one bug breaks every guardian.

3
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:29,600
Cowrie's pluggable CashuConsensusBox separates total-order finality from signing — effortless to operate standalone or on-chain.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:41,600
Byzantine guardian forging shares? Bilinear pairing checks reject it in real time while 4-of-5 keeps issuing.

5
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:53,600
No NUT-12 DLEQ bloat: 32.6% smaller cashuB tokens, 1.2ms offline verify, and 4.8x faster batch settlement.

6
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:04,600
One shared Blind-Seal threshold core powers both Cashu and Fedimint — unified guardians, two eCash ecosystems.

7
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:14,800
Open source, 25/25 tests passing, ready to run locally or on Fly.io. Try Cowrie today.
